cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "CA-ZTCF: Coexistence-Aware Zero Trust Continuity Framework (research prototype)"
abstract: >-
  A service-domain Zero Trust continuity function that re-evaluates IoT device trust at
  5G/WiFi access transitions using only evidence each access domain can realistically
  expose, without cross-domain identifier sharing. Developed as the software artefact of a
  master's thesis in Computer Networks Engineering.

  This release carries the frozen experimental evidence: 2160 runs across fifteen scenarios
  and three decision strategies, thirty paired repetitions each, executed on a reproducible
  software-based 5G/WiFi coexistence testbed (Open5GS with UERANSIM, and mac80211_hwsim
  with hostapd). Both radios are simulated, so nothing in it supports a claim about RF
  propagation, interference, channel quality or physical handover.
type: software
version: 1.0.1
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
